@startuml owned-resource-lifecycle-state
' ============================================================================
' OwnedDictionaryResource / ResourceContext lifecycle — the retain ledger.
' Source of truth: src/bindings.rs (OwnedDictionaryResource::new / as_raw /
' Drop; resource_retain / resource_release; dictionary_snapshot's
' std::mem::forget transfer). The count is the Arc<ResourceContext> strong
' count (Collins 1960 reference counting).
' Color key (ABI concept colors):
'   #DCEDC8 + #33691E producer-owned handle states
'   #FFECB3 + #FF6F00 states with foreign-held (leased) retains
'   #FFCDD2 + #B71C1C undefined-behavior warning
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam wrapWidth 160
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #ECEFF1
skinparam noteBorderColor #90A4AE
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #37474F
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}

title OwnedDictionaryResource lifecycle — every stored copy is one retain;\nthe last release destroys the context

state "ProducerOwned\nstrong = 1" as ProducerOwned #DCEDC8 : the Rust guard\n(OwnedDictionaryResource)\nowns the only retain
state "CoOwned\nstrong = 1 + n, n ≥ 1" as CoOwned #FFECB3 : guard retain plus n\nforeign stored copies
state "ForeignOwned\nstrong = n ≥ 1" as ForeignOwned #FFECB3 : every remaining retain\nis foreign-held
state "Destroyed" as Destroyed #FFFFFF : ResourceContext dropped;\npayload Arc released;\nbackend freed with its\nlast co-owner

[*] --> ProducerOwned : OwnedDictionaryResource::new\n(handle construction · resource())\nstrong := 1 — **born with one retain**

ProducerOwned --> ProducerOwned : as_raw() — borrow of the two\nwords, **no retain** (copy-not-retain)
ProducerOwned --> CoOwned : foreign vtable.retain\n(consumer stores a copy)
CoOwned --> CoOwned : further retain / release\nwhile both sides hold ≥ 1
CoOwned --> ProducerOwned : last foreign release
CoOwned --> ForeignOwned : guard dropped\n(ldict_dictionary_free) —\nDrop releases the guard retain
ProducerOwned --> ForeignOwned : dictionary_snapshot export:\nstd::mem::forget hands the\nborn retain to the consumer
ProducerOwned --> Destroyed : guard dropped —\nstrong 1 → 0
ForeignOwned --> ForeignOwned : foreign retain / release\nwhile strong stays ≥ 1
ForeignOwned --> Destroyed : last foreign release —\nstrong 1 → 0
Destroyed --> [*]

note bottom of ForeignOwned #FFECB3
  This state is why a retained resource
  **outlives** ldict_dictionary_free: the
  consumer's leased references keep the
  captured payload alive.
end note

note bottom of Destroyed #FFCDD2
  **After zero there is no recovery.** A release
  without a matching retain, or any vtable call
  after the last release, is undefined behavior —
  the producer cannot detect it. The ledger
  invariant is the consumer's proof obligation:
  releases ≤ retains on every path, exactly
  equal at the end.
end note
@enduml
